From: Johannes Meyer zum Alten Borgloh <code@jzab.de>
Subject: [PATCH] [img-boot] Let the device spec set the release

Release is always 1. On OBS that does not matter, because OBS replaces
it with its own build counter, but a local rebuild of
droid-hal-<device>-img-boot with the same kernel sublevel keeps the
version-release of the installed package, so zypper does not see it as
an update. A device spec that pins droid-hal's images to the build it
packed then also keeps requiring the old droid-hal version-release,
which blocks the droid-hal upgrade.

Take the release from img_boot_release when the device spec defines it,
for example as a build stamp like droid-hal's rel_date. Without it the
release stays 1, so existing specs are unaffected.

Applies to mer-hybris/hybris-initrd 7b972b6. droid-hal-img-boot-pdx246
ships the result as the override initrd-pdx246/droid-hal-device-img-boot.inc;
tools/check-initrd-overrides.sh checks that the two agree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 droid-hal-device-img-boot.inc | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/droid-hal-device-img-boot.inc b/droid-hal-device-img-boot.inc
index 1984489..26d035d 100644
--- a/droid-hal-device-img-boot.inc
+++ b/droid-hal-device-img-boot.inc
@@ -181,7 +181,10 @@ Version:    0.0.1
 %else
 Version:    %{localver}
 %endif
-Release:    1
+# The device spec can set the release, e.g. to a build stamp, so that a
+# local rebuild upgrades the installed package. OBS replaces the release
+# with its own build counter anyway.
+Release:    %{?img_boot_release}%{!?img_boot_release:1}
 License:    GPLv2
 Source0:    %{name}-%{version}.tar.bz2
 
